how much money did it take to bring  willem dafoe back as the green goblin  you may be surprised to hear that wasn't  the only thing he asked for  what  as fans debate where spider-man no way  home falls in the hierarchy of  spider-man movies one thing is clear  it's hands down the most ambitious  spidey flick to date without getting  into spoilers the film doesn't bother  itself with following formulas of the  past instead of having the web slinger  go up against a new baddie from the  comics the marvel cinematic universe's  peter parker has to face multiple  villains from previous spider-man  franchises it's an impressive feat to  get the original actors who played these  characters back after over a decade  since they originally put on the suits  what exactly did it take to convince  these actors to assume their villainous  personas once again in one interview  alfred molina who returned to play  doctor octopus jokingly kept it real by  saying for me it's just about the money  however willem dafoe had another reason  for returning as norman osborne aka the  green goblin although we're sure money  played a role for him too prior to the  release of no way home defoe made it  clear in an interview with mulderville  that if he were going to come back he  would do his own stunts we are who we  choose to be  these days it would have been easy to  cgi willem dafoe's face into a couple of  action scenes and call it a day but in  no way home the flesh in blood to foe  actually becomes a formidable presence  in fact many would likely refer to him  as the primary antagonist of the movie  seeing how the bulk of the destruction  comes from him and his influence on the  other villains and defoe's there for  much of the action doing his own fight  scenes at the age of 66. according to  dafoe that was an integral part of his  return he didn't just want to be a  glorified cameo he wanted the audience  to know he was there and doing his own  stunts as he told mulderville to do this  physical stuff was important to me in  fact one of the first things i said to  john watts and amy pascal basically when  they pitched it to me before there was  even a script was listen i don't want to  just pop in there as a cameo or just  fill in close-ups i want to do the  action because that's fun for me however  the need to do his own action extended  beyond just having fun he felt that  putting his actual body on the line was  integral to his process in getting the  best performance possible as he shared  in the interview it's really impossible  to add any integrity or any fun to the  character if you don't participate in  these things because all of that action  stuff informs your relationships to the  characters and the story it makes you  earn your right to play the character in  a funny way  you know how much i sacrificed after  seeing the movie fans would agree dafoe  was right at this point he's more than  earned the right to call himself the  preeminent green goblin and you can see  him in action now and spider-man no way  home  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

